00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.910
Let's first talk about homestead exemptions.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:38.610
A homestead exemption is a legal declaration
that lets you say this home I own.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.070
This is my primary residence.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.080
It is where I am sheltered.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:48.420
And in exchange for such a declaration, the
value of your home is protected from property

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:54.500
tax claims, from creditors, from forced sales
and a number of other circumstances.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:01.980
In normal cases, the way debt works in the
US is that you can have situations where you

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:07.499
could be forced to sell an asset to pay off
a creditor or a debt that you owe.

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:12.539
A homestead exemption or declaration lets
you say, this property is my home, this is

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.020
my residence, this is where I live.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.060
It's not a second home.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.560
It's not an investment property.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:24.130
And so by declaring it a homestead, you can't
be forced to sell that home to pay your debts.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.560
They can't leave you homeless to pay your
debts.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:33.299
This is separate from foreclosure, but it's
a very particular type of declaration.

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:38.320
In some states, only some portion of the home's
value is protected and that amount can vary.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.149
Texas has no dollar value limit.

00:01:40.149 --> 00:01:41.249
Some states do.

00:01:41.249 --> 00:01:45.899
And additionally, many states give you a tax
break because you do not have to pay property

00:01:45.899 --> 00:01:48.079
taxes on some portion of your home's value.

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:52.979
So if a certain state exempts one hundred
thousand dollars of value with a homestead

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:58.240
declaration, if the house is worth five hundred
K, but one hundred K is exempt, you pay property

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.709
taxes as if the house were worth only four
hundred thousand.

00:02:01.709 --> 00:02:04.020
OK, but here's the rule.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.020
